A||||9||GeeDee86GT||Front Battery....gas vent||||5||
Z||000000||GeeDee86GT||01-30-2001||08:46 PM||||Some of the posts on front mounted batteries have suggested a problem in venting gas released by the battery.  Would a sealed battery case with a tube spliced into the drain tube (from under windshield) be sufficient? Would a small pipe with an internal fan (occasionally switched on by switch) be better.<BR>Gary<BR>2 86 SE's 2.8||||reg||5
Z||000001||rockcrawl||01-30-2001||09:39 PM||||You'd better make sure you use a brushless fan or else it will be the perfect ignitor for your hydrogen bomb. Why not use a sealed gelled acid battery such as the ones Optima makes. they're expensive as hell, but it would eliminate any possibility of explosion. Plus you'd have a better battery to boot! On the other hand, a maintenence free battery with a tube connected to the vent should also work fine.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||01-31-2001||11:32 AM||||I would use an optima Battery. It's sealed & doesn't vent.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||01-31-2001||12:20 PM||||Those Optima batteries are awesome and are completeley sealed (possibly a gel-cell?), but expensive. First off, the spare tire compartment is not sealed, there is a small drain hole in the bottom. With my front battery mounting kit, there are also two large holes for the cables to route through, thus adding even more ventilation. If you are using a newish battery in good condition, the risk of fumes building up would be very minimal indeed. Running a vent tube to the outside would be good insurance, nonetheless.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Archie||01-31-2001||04:41 PM||||Why don't we just cut a hole in the hood, say 5" square?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>That's a joke.....<P>Seriously, I've been running front mounted batteries for about 13 years now and have not had a problem. Sometimes it's like being in a room full of old ladies, worrying about everything. When I use a front mount battery, I run the cables under the car on either side of the gas tank. When bringing these cables into the front compartment it's necessary to drill a couple of holes to route the cables thru.<P>HOLES = Vents<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000005||GeeDee86GT||01-31-2001||07:14 PM||||Thanks, guys. I thought about the Hydrogen/electric motor thing as soon as I pushed the post button, but what the hey. I could mount it in the passenger side and get rid of those pesky people always telling me to watch out for this and that.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||01-31-2001||07:47 PM||||I'm one of the people who brought that up...<P>Current battery technology doesn't gas like older ones did. My concern is that if there is a problem with the charging system or a cell short in the battery you could have allot of outgas. That gas needs a way out.<P>the optima orbital whatevers should present even less of an issue even with a charging system problem.||||reg||1
Z||000007||danny boy||02-01-2001||05:40 PM||||   Just as long as the cables are routed correctly I dont see a problem. Listen to you guys, Worried about gasses building up under the hood and not a thing was mentioned about the fact that the cables are UNDER THE CAR AND AGAINST THE GAS TANK!!! If those cables fray and spark the tank uh,oh. Or even worse,gas is leaking  from the tank,but no one knows it see, and this one time you drag over a speedbump,and the next thing you know your,well you wouldn't know anything them would you? And all because you wanted better weight distribution.<BR>   No, seriously, Ive had mine for 3 years and I've never had a problem with anything.||||reg||12
Z||000008||stsmithgt||02-01-2001||05:59 PM||||How bout a little scoop to ram fresh air into  the battery box and an exit vent. I could get a model car and borrow the scoop off that and put in on my hood......... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000009||terryk||02-01-2001||06:03 PM||||From my calculations, the hood is quite capable of containing the blast. Don't worry about it.||||reg||12
